  {
   "id": "40ff0824-7a75-4804-9072-807aaea18b04",
   "name": "Sticky Note e92c9ffa",
   "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
   "typeVersion": 1,
   "position": [
    100,
    592
   ],
   "parameters": {
    "content": "SF8 v-next.7 - Approval View Sync (F32 + SF6 contacts + Yangon-first + People tab + lead_key). Publishes ranked scored leads into the v-next Sheet COPY keyed by a single composite lead_key (run_id|company_id) - the v-next.6 People fix applied to Lead Review per Wonder FIX-2, because appendOrUpdate batch matching on a shared first key column corrupted rows. Phone/Facebook/Email/Size columns (SF6), ordered Yangon -> Mandalay -> Bangkok -> other (city from the Places record), then a People tab keyed by person_key. Header gate: run_id, company_id, Decision, Note, lead_key must exist on the copy or zero rows are written and a Gmail draft names the missing header. Decision and Note columns are never written. insufficient_data rows show as Unknown - insufficient data (F31).",
    "color": 5
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "6bc30193-c1c3-4031-ab18-5af950963370",
   "name": "When Executed by Another Workflow",
   "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
   "typeVersion": 1.1,
   "position": [
    40,
    400
   ],
   "parameters": {
